# Bounded pool host staging and per-UUID lease lifecycle

Bounded host block-staging arena (`PoolStagingStorage` in `KVCacheManagerBase`)
and per-UUID page-lease registration lifecycle in
`KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::PoolReshardRegisterRecv` (`docs/transfer/reshard.md`
§Boundaries). Host *layer* slot multiplexing (`StagingLayerManager`) is modelled
separately in `Transfer/LayerStaging.lean`.

File aliases: `base.{h,cc}` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_base.{h,cc}`,
`mgr.cc` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer.cc`,
`pool_staging_test.cc` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/pool_staging_test.cc`,
`pool_reshard_test.cc` = `tpu_sync/kv_cache/kv_cache_manager_with_transfer_pool_reshard_test.cc`.

## State

`PoolStagingStorage` mutations run under `KVCacheManagerBase::staging_mu_`;
`sessions_` and `pending_pool_reshard_recvs_` run under `KVCacheManagerWithTransfer::mu_`:

| Field | C++ | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `Arena.numSlots` | `PoolStagingStorage::num_slots` (`ConfigurePoolStaging`) | bounded page slots (`staging_leases * blocks_per_lease < num_blocks`; else full mirror) |
| `Arena.freeSlots` | `PoolStagingStorage::free_slots` | unleased slot stack (`0 .. num_slots - 1` pop order) |
| `Arena.leases` | `PoolStagingStorage::leases[uuid]` (`PoolStagingLease`) | per-UUID `slot_by_block` map and allocated `slots` |
| `RegState.activeSessions` | `ReshardReceiveSession` entries in `sessions_` | active UUIDs and their required block IDs |
| `RegState.inFlightArms` | `PoolReshardRegisterRecv` calls between Phase 1 and Phase 3 | tracks `pending_pool_reshard_recvs_` claims and Phase 2 leases |

## Events

Parameterized on `RegState` by `RegistrationPolicy` (`.reserveBeforeLease` shipping vs.
`.leaseBeforeReserve` mutant):

| Event | C++ |
|---|---|
| `beginArm callId uuid blocks` | Phase 1 (`PoolReshardRegisterRecv`, manager `mu_`): retire settled incumbent, refuse live one, and under `.reserveBeforeLease` claim `uuid` in `pending_pool_reshard_recvs_` |
| `acquireArmLease callId` | Phase 2 (`CreateReshardReceiveSession` → `AcquireStagingLeases` → `AcquirePoolStagingLease`, `staging_mu_`): idempotently lease missing blocks, or release and clear claim on failure |
| `finishArm callId` | Phase 3 (`PoolReshardRegisterRecv`, manager `mu_`): drop pending claim and seat `sessions_[uuid]` (under `.leaseBeforeReserve`, duplicate refusal destroys temporary session and frees `leases[uuid]`) |
| `settleSession uuid` | session settlement + `CompleteReadWithDetails` retirement and post-poll `ReleasePoolStagingLeases(uuid)` |

## Assumptions

* **A1 (fresh UUIDs across poll cleanup).** `CompleteReadWithDetails` filters `retired_uuids`
  against `sessions_` and `pending_pool_reshard_recvs_` under manager `mu_` and calls
  `ReleasePoolStagingLeases(uuid)` after unlocking; `settleSession` assumes a retiring `uuid`
  is not concurrently re-registered during that unlocked cleanup (`Reshard/Coordinator.lean`).

## Not modelled

* **Timed wait in `AcquirePoolStagingLease`.** Waiting on `staging_cv_` up to
  `pool_staging_lease_timeout()` while holding earlier storage leases or caller ops is
  collapsed: `Arena.acquireLease = none` covers immediate over-capacity and timeout alike.
* **Send registration (`PoolReshardPush`).** `PoolReshardPush` checks `sessions_` and seats
  `sessions_[uuid]` in separate `mu_` scopes with no `pending_pool_reshard_recvs_` counterpart;
  concurrent sends sharing one `uuid` are assumed absent (`Reshard/Send.lean` A2).

## Properties

* **`acquireLease_idempotent`** (`missingBlocksAux_empty_of_covered`): re-acquiring
  already-leased block IDs on a shared `storage_index` for the same `uuid` is a no-op.
* **`ArenaInv.conservation` & `allocateMissing_slot_sum`**: total slots across `freeSlots`
  and active leases equals `numSlots`.
* **`no_slot_aliasing_between_distinct_uuids`**: distinct active `uuid`s hold disjoint slot
  lists and never resolve any block IDs to the same staging slot.
* **`reachable_reserveBeforeLease_safe`**: under `.reserveBeforeLease`, every reachable state
  keeps active receive sessions' leases live and pairwise slot-disjoint (`ActiveSessionsHoldLeases`),
  whereas `.leaseBeforeReserve` fails (`trace_duplicate_uuid_frees_survivor_lease_and_aliases_slot`).

